# Every file in this repository is checked out with LF endings, on every
# platform, because two things here break on CRLF and only one of them is
# cosmetic.
#
# `gofmt -l .` reports a CRLF Go file as unformatted, so a Git-for-Windows
# checkout — which converts to CRLF by default — failed the entire Windows test
# job on line endings alone, before it ran a single test.
#
# The one that matters: handler.py is embedded into the binary and executed by
# python3 on a target, and the shell fragments beside it are sent to a POSIX
# shell. A Windows operator building from source would otherwise ship CRLF onto
# somebody else's machine, which is a footprint waldo promises not to leave.
* text=auto eol=lf
